Ok - I think this might be a new trick.  Certainly someone here will
let me know otherwise.



You need three things to make this work:

1) a dunce cap
2) a way to lose levels such as the healer's artifact staff, the spell
of drain life or Stormbringer
3) a reliable way to remove curses (likely holy water)

Bonus items:
Potions of gain level, extra/full healing, ring(s) of gain
constitution, high intrinsic wisdom, enchanted helm of brilliance, a
way to create monsters, lots of nice gear to keep you safe and combat
effective at lvl1

Ok here is the essence of the trick:  Nethack does not remember how
many HPs and energy you get each time you level.  If you get level
drained it can't just back out the HP and energy you gained for the
last level - instead it just guesses based on your current stats.  HPs
gained is based on constitution (but only a little) and for energy it's
related to wisdom/2 both with a random element.  The exploit is that
you make sure your wisdom is high on the way up and low on the way
down.  This will bias the net gains and losses to the positive.

Practical example:
You have the Staff of Aesculapius (cap and staff = early wish?), are
lvl 10, have a dunce cap and 8 holy waters.  You are on Dlvl1 on an
Elbereth burned space and have -10 AC.  There are a handful of trash
monsters on the level.

Put on dunce cap - it auto curses and int+wis are set to 6 from 17.
Remove all constitution and wisdom raising items (only HoB comes to
mind for wis and it uses same slot as the cap).  Throw staff up over
and over letting it lvl drain you until down to lvl 1 (but don't kill
yourself by accident!).  This is a good time to buy protection too if
you have safe passage to a priest.

Now uncurse the cap with holy water and remove it, put on your best
gear for constitution and wisdom such as a +3 HoB and a +2 gain cons
(taking you from 16 to 18).  Regen with staff if HPs get too low.  If
low enough on HP and safe to pray - pray for increase of max HP (might
also uncurse the cap which could be useful).  At this point you start
leveling up again.  It should be easy to get to lvl 6 or so on
relatively easy, safe stuff.  Brown puddings would be handy...

Rinse, repeat.  The only thing lost is holy water.  Taking wisdom from
6 to 20 is worth an average of 7 energy per lvl (difference divided by
2) or 30-40 per cycle.

Feels dirty doesn't it?  I wizard tested it and it works.

I don't have a great strategy for constitution and HP varies less with
a change in that stat but a +2 ring taking you from 16 to 18 is worth 2
HP on average per lvl.  Cursed and blessed unihorns work to change
stats, but slowly, randomly and with other effects.  Perhaps there are
other variations on this theme?



